    "Half a count" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "نصف حركة"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Half a tanween is neither the joined reading nor the stopped one." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "نصف تنوين ليس قراءة وصل ولا قراءة وقف."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Half always means through the father." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "غير الأشقاء هنا من جهة الأب دائمًا."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Half here always means through the father: a maternal half-brother's sons and a maternal uncle are not among these residuaries. The nearest of these takes whatever the fixed shares leave and shuts out everyone below him.\n\nA sister's children and a daughter's children are outside these rules too: they inherit as dhawu al-arham, once nobody above them survives." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "غير الأشقاء هنا من جهة الأب دائمًا: فأبناء الأخ لأم والخال ليسوا من هؤلاء العصبة. وأقربهم يأخذ ما أبقته الفروض، ويحجب كل من دونه.\n\nوأولاد الأخت وأولاد البنت خارج هذه الأحكام أيضًا: فهم يرثون بوصفهم من ذوي الأرحام، إذا لم يبقَ أحد ممن فوقهم."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Half here always means through the father: a maternal half-brother's sons are not heirs at all, and neither is a maternal uncle. The nearest of these takes whatever the fixed shares leave and shuts out everyone below him. A sister's children and a daughter's children are outside these rules too: they inherit as dhawu al-arham, once nobody above them survives." : {},
