          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light (muraqqaq) rāʾ" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "الراء المرقّقة"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light Concealment" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "إخفاء مرقّق"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light Ikhfaa partially hides noon or tanween before certain letters with a lighter nasal ghunnah." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "الإخفاء المرقّق يُخفي النون الساكنة أو التنوين جزئيًا قبل حروف معيّنة بغنة أخف."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light Laam (After Kasrah)" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "اللام المرقّقة (بعد الكسرة)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light Marks" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "تشكيل خفيف"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light Raa" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "الراء المرقّقة"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light a subject across the whole Quran" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "أضئ موضوعًا عبر القرآن كله"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light against heavy, three times. The tip of the tongue stays put and only the back of it moves." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "مرقق في مقابل مفخم، ثلاث مرات. طرف اللسان ثابت في موضعه، ولا يتحرك إلا أقصاه."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light and Darkness" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "النور والظلمات"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light and heavy partners" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "أزواج المرقق والمفخم"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light echo" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "نبرة مرققة"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light either way. Stopping leaves a sakin ك before the ra, and the ذ before that carries a kasrah." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "مرققة في الحالين. فالوقف يترك قبل الراء كافًا ساكنة، والذال قبلها مكسورة."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light hum then heavy hum, with the same noon before each." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "غنة رقيقة ثم غنة مفخمة، والنون واحدة قبل كل منهما."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light joined, on its kasrah, and light stopped as well, because a ya sakinah sits before it." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "مرققة في الوصل على كسرتها، ومرققة في الوقف أيضًا لأن قبلها ياءً ساكنة."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light letter (Muraqqaq)" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "حرف مرقَّق"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light letter (ك)" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "حرف مرقّق (ك)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light letter (ن)" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "حرف مرقّق (ن)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light more subjects" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "أضئ مزيدًا من الموضوعات"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light ra: kasrah, or sakin after an original kasrah" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "راء مرقّقة: كسرة، أو ساكنة بعد كسرة أصلية"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light when the ra carries a kasrah or a kasratan: شَرِّ, غَيۡرِ, رِزۡقٗا. Again the shadda is irrelevant: شَرِّ is doubled and light throughout." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "وترقق إذا كانت مكسورة أو منونة بالكسر: شَرِّ، غَيۡرِ، رِزۡقٗا. والشدة هنا أيضًا لا أثر لها: فشَرِّ مشددة ومرققة في شطريها جميعًا."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light when you read on. Stop here and the ra turns heavy: the ج is sakin and the ف before it has a fatha." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "مرققة إذا وصلت. فإن وقفت هنا فُخِّمت الراء: فالجيم ساكنة والفاء قبلها مفتوحة."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light, because مَرۡضَاتِ ends on a kasrah. Note it, then read on to the next example in the same ayah." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "ترقيق، لأن مَرۡضَاتِ آخرها كسرة. تنبه لها ثم واصل إلى المثال التالي في الآية نفسها."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light: after a kasrah" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "ترقيق: بعد كسرة"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Light: the noon sits before a waaw, so assume a damma, \"noo\"" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "نور: النون قبل الواو، فافترض ضمة: «نُو»"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Lightening the ra of ٱرۡجِعُوٓاْ because a kasrah is heard just before it." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "ترقيق راء ٱرۡجِعُوٓاْ لأن كسرة تُسمَع قبلها."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Lightly hide noon or tanween with nasal." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "إخفاء النون الساكنة أو التنوين مع غنة مرقّقة."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Like the b in “book”." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "كصوت b في “book”."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Like the d in “door”, with the tongue on the back of the upper front teeth." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "كصوت d في “door”، وطرف اللسان على باطن الثنايا العليا."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Like the f in “fan”." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "كصوت f في “fan”."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Like the h in “hat”, a soft breath (haa, not the deep Haa)." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "كصوت h في “hat”، نفَس خفيف (هاء، لا الحاء العميقة)."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Like the j in “jam”." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "كصوت j في “jam”."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Like the k in “king”." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "كصوت k في “king”."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Like the l in “lamp”." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "كصوت l في “lamp”."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Like the m in “moon”." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "كصوت m في “moon”."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Like the n in “noon”." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "كصوت n في “noon”."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Like the previous rule, this one only operates across two words. And like the previous rule, the mushaf tells you it is happening: no sukoon on the noon, a shadda on the ل or ر." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "وهذا الحكم كسابقه لا يجري إلا بين كلمتين. وهو كسابقه أيضًا مبيَّن في المصحف: لا سكون على النون، وشدة على اللام أو الراء."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Like the s in “sun”." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "كصوت s في “sun”."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Like the sh in “ship”." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "كصوت sh في “ship”."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Like the t in “table”, but with the tongue on the back of the upper front teeth rather than behind them." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "كصوت t في “table”، لكن طرف اللسان يلامس باطن الثنايا العليا، لا ما وراءها."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Like the th in “this” or “mother” (the voiced one), never the th in “three”." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "كصوت th في “this” أو “mother” (المجهور)، لا th في “three” أبدًا."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Like the th in “three” or “think” (the breathy one), never the th in “this”." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "كصوت th في “three” أو “think” (المهموس)، لا th في “this” أبدًا."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Like the w in “water” as a consonant; as a vowel it is the “oo” of “food”." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "كصوت w في “water” إذا كانت حرفًا صامتًا؛ وإذا كانت حرف مدّ فهي “oo” في “food”."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Like the y in “yes” as a consonant; as a vowel it is the “ee” of “see”." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "كصوت y في “yes” إذا كانت حرفًا صامتًا؛ وإذا كانت حرف مدّ فهي “ee” في “see”."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Like the z in “zebra”." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "كصوت z في “zebra”."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Likely Laylatul Qadr" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "ليلة القدر المرجّحة"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Lin" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "اللين"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Lin is ease, not length. The stretch belongs to the madd chapter and only applies at a stop." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "اللين سهولة لا طول. والمد من باب المدود ولا يكون إلا في الوقف."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Lin on the و: sakin, with a fatha before it. Read on into ٱلدِّينِ and it is a pure glide, with no effort from the tongue and no stretch." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "لين في الواو: ساكنة وقبلها فتحة. لا كلفة على اللسان ولا مد."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Lin. No effort and no stretch when you read straight on." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "لين. لا كلفة ولا مد عند وصل القراءة."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Lin: sakin after a fatha" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "اللين: ساكنة بعد فتحة"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Lin: و and ي sakin after a fatha, with no effort and no stretch." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "اللين: الواو والياء الساكنتان بعد فتحة، بغير كلفة وبغير مد."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Linguistically, the word tajweed comes from the Arabic root ج-و-د (j-w-d), meaning \"to improve,\" \"to make excellent,\" or \"to perfect.\" In the context of the Quran, it means reciting the words of Allah as they were revealed precisely, clearly, and with care." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "التجويد لغةً من الجذر ج-و-د، ومعناه التحسين والإجادة والإتقان. وفي سياق القرآن هو تلاوة كلام الله كما أُنزل، بدقة ووضوح وعناية."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Lining up the riwayat…" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "جارٍ محاذاة الروايات…"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Lip Movement" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "حركة الشفتين"
