            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "الطرف فوق الثنايا السفلى"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Tip at the Roots of the Teeth" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "الطرف مع أصول الثنايا"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Tip contact produces a د or a ظ. ض is the only letter made with the edge against the upper molars, and the only one whose sound runs along the length of that edge, the attribute called istitalah. It is the letter Arabic is named after." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "الاتصال بالطرف يُنتج دالا أو ظاء. والضاد هي الحرف الوحيد في اللغة الذي يخرج من الحافة، وهي الحرف الذي سميت به العربية."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Tip of the Tongue" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "طرف اللسان"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Tip of tongue: ت د ط ن ل ر س ز ص ث ذ ظ" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "طرف اللسان: ت د ط ن ل ر س ز ص ث ذ ظ"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Tip out on the teeth, then tip back behind them. If the second of each pair whistles and the first does not, both are right." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "الطرف خارجا على الأسنان، ثم الطرف راجعا خلفها. فإن صفر الثاني من كل زوج ولم يصفر الأول فكلاهما صواب."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Tip with the base of the front teeth" : {
