    "Waw (و) preceded by dammah" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "واو (و) قبلها ضمّة"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Waw after a damma in دُو. The lips round for the damma and stay rounded right through the hold. The word sits in the middle of the ayah and a vowelled ن follows the waw, so nothing can add to those two counts." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "واو بعد ضمة في رُو. تستدير الشفتان للضمة وتبقيان مستديرتين طول الإمساك."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Waw madd, then a stopped noon. The same ayah ending repeats in the next ayah, so mismatched lengths are audible immediately." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "واو مدٍّ ثمّ نون موقوف عليها. ورأس الآية نفسه يتكرّر في الآية التالية، فيُسمع اختلاف المقدار فورًا."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Waw madd, then a stopped ra. Joined, the ra is light because of its kasra; stop and the kasra is gone, so the sakin waw hands the ra back to the damma before it and the ra turns heavy." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "واو مدٍّ قبل راء موقوف عليها. ورقّق الراء هنا كما تقتضي كسرتها."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Waw sakinah preceded by dammah (ـُو)" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "الواو الساكنة المضموم ما قبلها (ـُو)"
          }
        }
      }
    },
