    "‎ٱسۡمَ  ->  isma" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "ٱسۡمَ"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "‎ٱل begins with a fatha; the seven heard nouns and the masdars begin with a kasra." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "ٱل يُبتدأ بها بالفتح، والأسماء السبعة يُبتدأ بها بالكسر."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "‎ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ is heavy throughout and شَرِّ is light throughout. A shadda is length, not a second letter." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "ٱلرَّحۡمَٰنِ مفخمة في شطريها وشَرِّ مرققة في شطريها. والشدة زمن لا حرف ثانٍ."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "‎ٱلضَّآلِّينَ ends Surat al-Fatiha, so this error is repeated in every prayer a learner makes." : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "ٱلضَّآلِّينَ آخر سورة الفاتحة، فيتكرّر هذا الخطأ في كلّ صلاة يصلّيها المتعلّم."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "‎ٱلۡحَمۡدُ  ->  al-hamdu" : {
      "extractionState" : "manual",
      "localizations" : {
        "ar" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
